.TH ALX-ADDUSER 8 "November 2026" "Algothix OS 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
alx-adduser \- create a new Algothix OS user with ALX defaults and systemd memory limits
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B alx-adduser
\fIusername\fR [\fB\-\-admin\fR] [\fB\-\-memory\-max\fR \fIMiB\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B alx-adduser
creates a Linux user with \fI/etc/skel\fR ALX configs, \fBzsh\fR as default shell,
optional \fBsudo\fR group membership, and a per-UID systemd slice drop-in
(\fI/etc/systemd/system/user-<uid>.slice.d/50-alx-limits.conf\fR).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR alx-tune (8),
.BR alx-join-domain (8)
